        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "H2L was prepared by 1:1 condensation of 5-chloro-2-hydroxybenzaldehyde and (2-aminophenyl)methanol in hot methanol. A mixture of Co(OAc)2·4H2O (0.0248 g, 0.100 mmol), Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.0456 g, 0.100 mmol), H2L (0.0262 g, 0.100 mmol), NaOH (0.0040 g, 0.100 mmol), ethanol (1.5 mL) and DMF (0.5 mL) was sealed in an 8 mL Pyrex tube and heated at 90 °C for 3 days under autogenous pressure. Slow cooling to room temperature gave green-block crystals. The main text only states that 1 was obtained from Dy(NO3)3·6H2O, H2L and Co(OAc)2·4H2O in EtOH/DMF at 90 °C, without amounts.",
